@page "/docs/extensions/svg-chart-data-drag"

<Seo Canonical="/docs/extensions/svg-chart-data-drag" Title="Blazorise SVG Chart Data Point Dragging" Description="Learn how to edit native SVG chart values by dragging data points with pointer or keyboard input." />

<DocsPageTitle Path="Extensions/SVG Chart Data Point Dragging">
    Blazorise SVG Chart Data Point Dragging
</DocsPageTitle>

<DocsPageLead>
    Let users edit line, area, scatter, and bubble chart values directly in the chart.
</DocsPageLead>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Add <Code>SvgChartDataDrag</Code> to enable dragging declaratively, or configure <Code>SvgChartOptions.DataDrag</Code>. Line and area series support vertical dragging. Scatter and bubble series support <Code>X</Code>, <Code>Y</Code>, or <Code>XY</Code> dragging. Set <Code>Draggable</Code> to <Code>false</Code> on an individual series to exclude it.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Use <Code>XStep</Code> and <Code>YStep</Code> to snap values, <Code>CanDrag</Code> to filter individual points, and <Code>DragStarted</Code>, <Code>Dragging</Code>, and <Code>DragEnded</Code> to observe changes. Persist the final value to your data source in <Code>DragEnded</Code>. Tooltips are suppressed while dragging by default; set <Code>ShowTooltip</Code> to <Code>true</Code> to display a live value tooltip. Press an arrow key while a point is focused to adjust it, hold Shift for a larger step, or press Escape during pointer dragging to restore the original value.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Examples
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Editable forecast">
        Drag a forecast marker vertically. Values snap to increments of five, while the baseline series remains read-only.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="SvgChartDataDragExample" Outlined FullWidth>
        <SvgChartDataDragExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Limitations
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Data point dragging is not enabled for radial, bar, column, stacked, or streaming charts. Category positions on line and area charts remain fixed; use scatter or bubble data when the X value must also be editable.
</DocsPageParagraph>

